==Battleground==
*1 [[Director Kurosawah]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*1 [[Casaurian Darkjo]] spawns as the boss after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*3 [[Mooth]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 46.67~50 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 30~36.67 seconds<sup>900f~1,100f</sup>.
*10 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*3 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
[[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]] are great meatshields as usual, plus [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] can tank many hits from the Angelic Gories in this stage, while [[:Category:Behemoth Slayer Cats|Behemoth Slayer Cats]] help with their extra damage and chance to dodge. [[Ancient Egg: N103 (Rare Cat)|Gas Mask Cat]] is a very good meatshield for tanking from the Casaurian Darkjo, what with its Behemoth Slayer, [[Resistant|Resistance]] to [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemies, and [[Immune to Toxic|Immunity to Toxic]]. As for the Mooths, they tend to lag behind the main enemies, while also being your main cash source. [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Cats with Long Distance]] can be an effective way to kill them without wasting too much time. [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Cats with Wave Attacks]] can work, a great example is [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]], who can snipe the Mooths while slowly chipping the Kurosawah in the back. But be careful, for the fast attack speed of the Darkjo can mean a waste of money.

[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] can be a great asset here ONLY if you have his [[Wave Attack]] [[Talents|Talent]], since he can use the Angelic Gories as a stepping stone to snipe Darkjo and Kurosawah. However, due to his slow speed and terrible range, if you don't have his Wave Attack Talent, don't use him.

==Trivia==
*Venomous Duck's Japanese name, Deadly Poisonous Strange Bird (猛毒怪鳥 ''Mōdoku Kaichō''), is a reference to the title of ''Monster Hunter''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s [[wikia:monsterhunter:Gypceros|Gypceros]], Poison Strange Bird (毒怪鳥 ''Doku Kaichō'').

